35,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It is exactly as I suspected. The partition is practically transparent to sound, and the lack of a dedicated eating area is bleeding into our workspace. We are compromising our professional environment for convenience.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I saw the invoices. We've spent 68,000 yen on outside rentals last year because the room isn't working for us. It's... it's a lot of money to keep paying every month.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wow, you guys! I found out that only the people sitting by the door use the room all the time! And the fridge was a disaster—someone had to clean up everyone's mystery leftovers twice! That's not fair!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It seems we are suffering from more than just a lack of space. We have lost the sanctuary for our hearts; our difficult moments are public, and our new friends remain strangers. We must heal this.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The facilities data shows that maintenance is concentrated on equipment rooms, not the storage area. Combined with the outside hire costs @Daisuke mentioned, it's clear we are paying for space we don't have here.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Rin, your observation about the door is key. Since the wall is so thin, those of us sitting nearby are forced to hear everything. We need a solution that prioritizes soundproofing and hygiene.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I also looked at the fit-out quotes. One is 141,000 yen for a screen and table, and the other is 96,000 for a kitchen setup. I'm worried about who will have to sign for these costs.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, don't be worried! If we make the room awesome, it'll be worth it! But we have to make sure everyone helps clean up, or the fridge will just get gross again!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Money is but a tool, @Daisuke. What truly matters is the investment we make in each other. A space that allows us to speak honestly and bond deeply is priceless for our collective well-being.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the fit-out costs are a one-time expense, but we must consider the hidden costs of upkeep. If we install a kitchen, who manages the cleaning? We cannot afford to waste more hours on unpaid maintenance.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, your concern about maintenance is valid, but the current ""unpaid maintenance"" is already happening at our desks. We are literally working amidst crumbs. A dedicated space is the only logical way to stop the bleed.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I guess you're right, Shion. But 141,000 yen is still a lot... and the kitchen one is 96,000. I just don't want us to agree to something and then realize we can't actually afford it.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But we're already spending money on those outside rentals! @Daisuke, if we use that money to fix our own room, it's like a magic trick! We just have to make a real rule about cleaning!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, your spirit is as bright as a morning sun. Indeed, let us not fear the cost, but rather the cost of remaining strangers. We need a place where we can truly see one another.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, a rule is only as good as its enforcement. If we rely on goodwill for cleaning, we are simply shifting the burden. We need a solution that minimizes the time spent on upkeep.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Let's be realistic. We are currently paying for outside space while our office becomes a cafeteria. Whether we choose a professional screen or a kitchen, the priority must be separating the room's noise and mess from our desks.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I understand. If we keep paying for outside rooms, it just keeps adding up. Maybe a one-time cost is better than paying every month... I just hope we can all agree on which one is more important.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,I think we should pick the one that makes us the happiest! But we have to promise—no more mystery leftovers! Let's make a super-duper cleaning chart so it's fair for everyone!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Happiness is a beautiful goal, Rin, but let us remember that true joy comes from peace and understanding. We need a space that invites us to speak our truths and welcome our new colleagues.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"We must avoid a solution that creates a permanent chore for one person. If we prioritize a professional setup over a kitchen, we reduce the maintenance burden and the risk of hygiene issues. Efficiency should be our primary metric.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
